# Gate step 1243-yiyq — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq).
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS. scripts/loop-status-metrics-audit.sh parses each host's newest
# loop_status entry for its cycle-metrics block. It anchored on the literal
# `skippable: candidates=`; scripts/cycle-metrics.sh later began emitting
# `skippable: window=7d candidates=`. One interposed field broke every match for
# twelve days, and the audit reported every host as NOT-PASTING the whole time.
#
# WHY THAT WAS EXPENSIVE RATHER THAN UNTIDY. That output is the coordination
# skill's designated evidence for whether hosts paste their metrics, and the
# skill prescribes routing a plain ask to any host that does not. On 2026-09-17
# a coordinator read 23 of 23 stems NOT-PASTING, concluded the practice had died
# fleet-wide, RECORDED IT AS A HAZARD, repeated it in a landed commit message,
# wrote it into a packet's context as the reason cross-host evidence had been
# unavailable, and told a peer — who pasted because they were told the channel
# was dark. Every artifact downstream of a parser that had quietly gone blind.
#
# AND THE AUDIT LOOKED HEALTHY THROUGHOUT. It ends with `rows=N stems=N` and
# exits non-zero on a dropped stem. That check is real and it passed. It
# certifies ENUMERATION, not COMPREHENSION — a numeric agreement beside a
# verdict reads exactly like a self-check while the tool faithfully enumerates
# hosts it can no longer parse.
#
# THE TEETH ARE ARMS 1, 4 AND 6, and the mutation control was RUN, not assumed:
# against the pre-fix audit those three FAIL and the other three pass (they are
# regression guards, not teeth). Arm 1 pins that the audit reads what the
# emitter emits today. Arm 4 is what keeps arm 1 true next month: it extracts
# the audit's OWN SHAPE and runs the REAL cycle-metrics.sh output against it, so
# the two files cannot drift apart again silently. Arm 6 pins that a corpus with
# zero readable lines refuses with a FORMAT-DRIFT verdict instead of a
# fleet-behaviour claim — "no host is pasting" and "I cannot read any host" send
# a reader to opposite places and used to print identically.
#
# COST, MEASURED HERE 2026-09-17: 19.76 / 19.84 / 19.90 s. Essentially all of it
# is arm 4's single cycle-metrics.sh invocation; the five audit runs are cheap.
# That is the price of a BEHAVIOURAL tie. A source-grep for the format string
# would cost nothing and could not tell a format cycle-metrics.sh MENTIONS from
# one it EMITS, which is the exact distinction this defect turned on.
# `--no-repo-scan` was measured as an escape and is not one: 18.7s, and it emits
# no skippable line at all. NOT in the fast-refusal lane, whose admission rule
# is a median under one second.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path on purpose: a binding assembled from a
# variable is invisible to every name-based scan, including the
# bound-or-retired guard (1063-nraf). Keep it a plain string.
STEP_DESC="Checking the loop-status audit can still read what cycle-metrics emits (1243-yiyq)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-loop-status-audit-reads-current-emitter.sh"
STEP_ERROR="the loop-status audit and cycle-metrics.sh have drifted apart again (1243-yiyq) — the audit will report every host NOT-PASTING while parsing nothing; read which arm failed above"
STEP_OK="Loop-status audit parses the current emitter"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="macneo 2026-09-22 darwin ok:loop-status-audit-reads-current-emitter:6"
